WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.450
Weather planning begins with current official or otherwise approved sources appropriate to the location and operation.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:10.419
Review when the forecast was issued, the period it covers,

00:00:10.419 --> 00:00:15.182
and whether changing conditions are expected before, during, or after the mission.

00:00:15.182 --> 00:00:20.738
Check wind speed, gusts, direction, and expected changes at the surface and relevant altitude.

00:00:20.738 --> 00:00:25.501
A sheltered launch point may not represent conditions above trees, buildings, ridges,

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:26.691
or shoreline terrain.

00:00:26.691 --> 00:00:30.263
Review precipitation probability, type, timing, visibility, cloud, temperature, humidity,

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.438
and significant pressure or frontal changes where relevant.

00:00:33.438 --> 00:00:38.201
A percentage alone does not show whether rain will arrive during recovery

00:00:38.201 --> 00:00:40.582
or how intense it may be.

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:41.773
Consider local effects.

00:00:41.773 --> 00:00:47.329
Terrain can channel wind, water can produce fog or spray, buildings can create turbulence,

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:50.107
and sun-heated surfaces can generate unstable air.

00:00:50.107 --> 00:00:53.679
Prior site knowledge and an on-site check remain necessary.

00:00:53.679 --> 00:00:56.854
Forecast uncertainty should increase margin rather than confidence.

00:00:56.854 --> 00:01:01.220
When sources disagree or a front may arrive near recovery time,

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:05.983
choose the more conservative interpretation and shorten, delay, or relocate the mission.

00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:12.333
Define go or no-go criteria before travel and before organizational pressure to complete the flight increases.

00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:16.698
Criteria should reflect current rules, aircraft and payload guidance, crew experience,

00:01:16.698 --> 00:01:19.477
route complexity, return margin, and data-quality needs.

00:01:19.477 --> 00:01:23.445
Plan alternatives: a later time, shorter route, different authorized platform,

00:01:23.445 --> 00:01:25.827
ground inspection, existing imagery, or rescheduling.

00:01:25.827 --> 00:01:27.414
Document sources, assumptions, thresholds,

00:01:27.414 --> 00:01:31.780
and review time so the decision can be explained and updated.
